{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016npEnZBECPjcSHUwFVfbwH","type":"tool_result","content":"401\t### 8. Verification Engine\n402\t\n403\tThe verification engine keeps memory honest.\n404\t\n405\tVerification checks:\n406\t\n407\t- linked files still exist\n408\t- linked symbols still exist\n409\t- cited docs still exist\n410\t- linked tests still exist\n411\t- evidence text still matches when exact spans were captured\n412\t- implementation still matches memory claim where deterministic checks are possible\n413\t- contradicted/superseded states remain coherent\n414\t- branch-scoped memory is not leaking into unrelated branches\n415\t- time-bound memory has expired\n416\t\n417\tVerification outputs:\n418\t\n419\t- `verified`\n420\t- `unverified`\n421\t- `in_review`\n422\t- `stale`\n423\t- `contradicted`\n424\t- `superseded`\n425\t- `expired`\n426\t- `invalidated`\n427\t\n428\tVerification must be incremental and tied to workspace changes. Large repos cannot tolerate full rescans for every memory.\n429\t\n430\t### 9. MCP Surface\n431\t\n432\tThe MCP contract should expose high-level assistant workflows rather than forcing clients to compose low-level graph calls.\n433\t\n434\tRequired workflow tools:\n435\t\n436\t- `get_context_capsule`\n437\t- `prepare_change`\n438\t- `plan_edit`\n439\t- `trace_scenario`\n440\t- `diagnose_failure`\n441\t- `find_relevant_tests`\n442\t- `impact_from_diff`\n443\t- `get_docs_capsule`\n444\t- `get_backlinks`\n445\t- `expand_context`\n446\t- `get_working_set_context`\n447\t- `get_repo_playbook`\n448\t- `search_symbols`\n449\t- `search_memory`\n450\t- `record_workflow_outcome`\n451\t\n452\tNew or redesigned memory tools:\n453\t\n454\t- `get_task_memory`\n455\t- `save_memory`\n456\t- `propose_memory_evolution`\n457\t- `apply_memory_evolution`\n458\t- `verify_memory`\n459\t- `explain_memory`\n460\t- `list_memory_conflicts`\n461\t- `consolidate_session`\n462\t- `get_memory_metrics`\n463\t- `get_event_trace`\n464\t\n465\tTool surface discipline: ten new memory tools is a meaningful cognitive load for clients. Before shipping Phase 8, audit whether `propose_memory_evolution` + `apply_memory_evolution` can collapse into a single tool with an `action` parameter, and whether `verify_memory` + `explain_memory` can be unified. The goal is the smallest surface that covers all assistant workflows. Consolidate before stabilizing the MCP contract.\n466\t\n467\tEvery tool response should support:\n468\t\n469\t- compact rendering\n470\t- full structured JSON\n471\t- context handles\n472\t- stable expansion targets\n473\t- budget controls\n474\t- diagnostic explanations where useful\n475\t\n476\t### 10. Human Review Surface\n477\t\n478\tAgents are the primary client, but durable memory needs human inspectability.\n479\t\n480\tRequired operator views:\n481\t\n482\t- memory inbox\n483\t- proposed promotions\n484\t- proposed contradictions\n485\t- stale memory list\n486\t- memory evidence view\n487\t- event trace view\n488\t- retrieval explanation view\n489\t- usefulness metrics\n490\t- workspace graph health\n491\t- indexing health\n492\t- consolidation queue\n493\t\n494\tThis can be a VS Code extension panel or local web UI. It should be a review and trust surface, not the center of the product.\n495\t\n496\t## Storage Design\n497\t\n498\tUse SQLite as the durable local store unless proven insufficient. Split logical tables cleanly.\n499\t\n500\tCore tables:"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0696e093-0770-442b-8dc9-5393bbfcd0b6","uuid":"5f5ee526-7052-4abc-be02-d1ea2f823c1b","timestamp":"2026-05-17T13:03:25.105Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md","content":"### 8. Verification Engine\n\nThe verification engine keeps memory honest.\n\nVerification checks:\n\n- linked files still exist\n- linked symbols still exist\n- cited docs still exist\n- linked tests still exist\n- evidence text still matches when exact spans were captured\n- implementation still matches memory claim where deterministic checks are possible\n- contradicted/superseded states remain coherent\n- branch-scoped memory is not leaking into unrelated branches\n- time-bound memory has expired\n\nVerification outputs:\n\n- `verified`\n- `unverified`\n- `in_review`\n- `stale`\n- `contradicted`\n- `superseded`\n- `expired`\n- `invalidated`\n\nVerification must be incremental and tied to workspace changes. Large repos cannot tolerate full rescans for every memory.\n\n### 9. MCP Surface\n\nThe MCP contract should expose high-level assistant workflows rather than forcing clients to compose low-level graph calls.\n\nRequired workflow tools:\n\n- `get_context_capsule`\n- `prepare_change`\n- `plan_edit`\n- `trace_scenario`\n- `diagnose_failure`\n- `find_relevant_tests`\n- `impact_from_diff`\n- `get_docs_capsule`\n- `get_backlinks`\n- `expand_context`\n- `get_working_set_context`\n- `get_repo_playbook`\n- `search_symbols`\n- `search_memory`\n- `record_workflow_outcome`\n\nNew or redesigned memory tools:\n\n- `get_task_memory`\n- `save_memory`\n- `propose_memory_evolution`\n- `apply_memory_evolution`\n- `verify_memory`\n- `explain_memory`\n- `list_memory_conflicts`\n- `consolidate_session`\n- `get_memory_metrics`\n- `get_event_trace`\n\nTool surface discipline: ten new memory tools is a meaningful cognitive load for clients. Before shipping Phase 8, audit whether `propose_memory_evolution` + `apply_memory_evolution` can collapse into a single tool with an `action` parameter, and whether `verify_memory` + `explain_memory` can be unified. The goal is the smallest surface that covers all assistant workflows. Consolidate before stabilizing the MCP contract.\n\nEvery tool response should support:\n\n- compact rendering\n- full structured JSON\n- context handles\n- stable expansion targets\n- budget controls\n- diagnostic explanations where useful\n\n### 10. Human Review Surface\n\nAgents are the primary client, but durable memory needs human inspectability.\n\nRequired operator views:\n\n- memory inbox\n- proposed promotions\n- proposed contradictions\n- stale memory list\n- memory evidence view\n- event trace view\n- retrieval explanation view\n- usefulness metrics\n- workspace graph health\n- indexing health\n- consolidation queue\n\nThis can be a VS Code extension panel or local web UI. It should be a review and trust surface, not the center of the product.\n\n## Storage Design\n\nUse SQLite as the durable local store unless proven insufficient. Split logical tables cleanly.\n\nCore tables:","numLines":100,"startLine":401,"totalLines":969}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_017kwffjKLEKFeHbvi2RizTp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EeGLKu1dXXPxjxw6TJ5MBY","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md","offset":700,"limit":100},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1393,"cache_read_input_tokens":156104,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1393},"output_tokens":38,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0696e093-0770-442b-8dc9-5393bbfcd0b6","uuid":"0edc79bb-ae9f-48a4-b5dc-e69b509b7962","request_id":"req_011Cb8BoeZRKYsfszNWBtnt3"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EeGLKu1dXXPxjxw6TJ5MBY","type":"tool_result","content":"700\t\n701\t- completed tasks produce useful episode memories\n702\t- repeated successful traces produce procedural memories\n703\t- consolidation is auditable, reversible, and test-covered\n704\t\n705\t### Phase 7: Verification And Freshness\n706\t\n707\tDeliverables:\n708\t\n709\t- incremental memory verification against graph changes\n710\t- file/symbol/doc/test existence checks\n711\t- exact-span evidence validation where available\n712\t- branch and workspace scope enforcement\n713\t- time-bound expiry\n714\t- stale memory surfacing in workflow bundles\n715\t- verification jobs and operator diagnostics\n716\t\n717\tDefinition of done:\n718\t\n719\t- stale or contradicted memory cannot appear as normal trusted guidance\n720\t- verification results are explainable and queryable\n721\t\n722\t### Phase 8: Workflow Engine V2\n723\t\n724\tDeliverables:\n725\t\n726\t- redesigned versions of context, change planning, scenario tracing, failure diagnosis, docs retrieval, test selection, impact analysis, and playbook generation\n727\t- workflow composition over graph, event, memory, and working-memory substrates\n728\t- one-call edit-planning bundles with code, docs, tests, memory, risks, and verification commands\n729\t- workflow outcome recording integrated by default\n730\t\n731\tDefinition of done:\n732\t\n733\t- common coding tasks require fewer manual discovery calls\n734\t- workflows produce enough context to implement and verify changes without broad file dumping\n735\t\n736\t### Phase 9: Metrics And Evaluation\n737\t\n738\tDeliverables:\n739\t\n740\t- retrieval relevance metrics\n741\t- memory usefulness metrics\n742\t- context token efficiency metrics\n743\t- stale/contradicted memory surfacing metrics\n744\t- test-pass-after-plan metrics\n745\t- repeated-failure reduction metrics\n746\t- benchmark tasks with golden expected anchors\n747\t- regression dashboard or CLI report\n748\t\n749\tRequired metrics:\n750\t\n751\t- tool calls per successful task\n752\t- irrelevant files opened per task\n753\t- relevant anchor recall\n754\t- memory inclusion precision\n755\t- memory later-used rate\n756\t- stale memory surfaced rate\n757\t- contradiction missed rate\n758\t- tests recommended versus tests needed\n759\t- workflow success after first plan\n760\t\n761\tDefinition of done:\n762\t\n763\t- changes to retrieval, memory, and workflow behavior can be evaluated without relying on anecdote\n764\t\n765\t### Phase 10: Human Review And Extension UX\n766\t\n767\tDeliverables:\n768\t\n769\t- VS Code or local web review UI\n770\t- memory inbox\n771\t- promotion queue\n772\t- contradiction queue\n773\t- stale memory view\n774\t- event trace view\n775\t- retrieval explanation view\n776\t- consolidation job health\n777\t- indexing health\n778\t- one-click accept/reject for memory evolution proposals\n779\t\n780\tDefinition of done:\n781\t\n782\t- operators can understand and correct durable memory without reading raw SQLite rows\n783\t\n784\t### Phase 11: Hardening\n785\t\n786\tDeliverables:\n787\t\n788\t- large-repo performance tests\n789\t- concurrency tests\n790\t- recovery tests\n791\t- corrupted-event handling\n792\t- partial-index handling\n793\t- workspace-boundary tests\n794\t- migration tests\n795\t- MCP schema compatibility tests\n796\t- documentation for setup, operations, memory semantics, and workflow behavior\n797\t\n798\tDefinition of done:\n799\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0696e093-0770-442b-8dc9-5393bbfcd0b6","uuid":"f46aa9d0-c223-4733-aae3-eeea0ca42a31","timestamp":"2026-05-17T13:03:30.917Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md","content":"\n- completed tasks produce useful episode memories\n- repeated successful traces produce procedural memories\n- consolidation is auditable, reversible, and test-covered\n\n### Phase 7: Verification And Freshness\n\nDeliverables:\n\n- incremental memory verification against graph changes\n- file/symbol/doc/test existence checks\n- exact-span evidence validation where available\n- branch and workspace scope enforcement\n- time-bound expiry\n- stale memory surfacing in workflow bundles\n- verification jobs and operator diagnostics\n\nDefinition of done:\n\n- stale or contradicted memory cannot appear as normal trusted guidance\n- verification results are explainable and queryable\n\n### Phase 8: Workflow Engine V2\n\nDeliverables:\n\n- redesigned versions of context, change planning, scenario tracing, failure diagnosis, docs retrieval, test selection, impact analysis, and playbook generation\n- workflow composition over graph, event, memory, and working-memory substrates\n- one-call edit-planning bundles with code, docs, tests, memory, risks, and verification commands\n- workflow outcome recording integrated by default\n\nDefinition of done:\n\n- common coding tasks require fewer manual discovery calls\n- workflows produce enough context to implement and verify changes without broad file dumping\n\n### Phase 9: Metrics And Evaluation\n\nDeliverables:\n\n- retrieval relevance metrics\n- memory usefulness metrics\n- context token efficiency metrics\n- stale/contradicted memory surfacing metrics\n- test-pass-after-plan metrics\n- repeated-failure reduction metrics\n- benchmark tasks with golden expected anchors\n- regression dashboard or CLI report\n\nRequired metrics:\n\n- tool calls per successful task\n- irrelevant files opened per task\n- relevant anchor recall\n- memory inclusion precision\n- memory later-used rate\n- stale memory surfaced rate\n- contradiction missed rate\n- tests recommended versus tests needed\n- workflow success after first plan\n\nDefinition of done:\n\n- changes to retrieval, memory, and workflow behavior can be evaluated without relying on anecdote\n\n### Phase 10: Human Review And Extension UX\n\nDeliverables:\n\n- VS Code or local web review UI\n- memory inbox\n- promotion queue\n- contradiction queue\n- stale memory view\n- event trace view\n- retrieval explanation view\n- consolidation job health\n- indexing health\n- one-click accept/reject for memory evolution proposals\n\nDefinition of done:\n\n- operators can understand and correct durable memory without reading raw SQLite rows\n\n### Phase 11: Hardening\n\nDeliverables:\n\n- large-repo performance tests\n- concurrency tests\n- recovery tests\n- corrupted-event handling\n- partial-index handling\n- workspace-boundary tests\n- migration tests\n- MCP schema compatibility tests\n- documentation for setup, operations, memory semantics, and workflow behavior\n\nDefinition of done:\n","numLines":100,"startLine":700,"totalLines":969}}}
