{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012i33Y8jsUBnNWUA2Tf3yRd","type":"tool_result","content":"85\t- retrieval alignment\n86\t\n87\tDo not build opaque autonomous self-rewriting memory. Reflection should be inspectable, testable, and reversible.\n88\t\n89\t## Non-Negotiable Product Properties\n90\t\n91\t- Local-first by default.\n92\t- Deterministic identities for every file, symbol, doc section, event, and memory.\n93\t- Every durable memory has evidence.\n94\t- Every retrieved memory has an inclusion reason.\n95\t- Every stale or contradicted memory is surfaced as such, not hidden behind recency.\n96\t- Every workflow bundle is compact by default with deliberate expansion handles.\n97\t- Every background consolidation pass is recoverable, replayable, and observable.\n98\t- Every public MCP contract is documented and regression-tested.\n99\t- No silent broad workspace reads that bypass ignore rules or workspace boundaries.\n100\t- No unbounded graph traversal, payload growth, or event-log scans on hot paths.\n101\t\n102\t## System Architecture\n103\t\n104\t### 1. Ingestion Layer\n105\t\n106\tResponsibilities:\n107\t\n108\t- watch workspace changes\n109\t- parse code\n110\t- parse docs\n111\t- parse config and build files\n112\t- ingest test results and diagnostics\n113\t- capture assistant event traces\n114\t- normalize all inputs into stable records\n115\t\n116\tRequired inputs:\n117\t\n118\t- source files\n119\t- Markdown docs\n120\t- repo instruction files\n121\t- test files and test manifests\n122\t- package/build metadata\n123\t- compiler diagnostics\n124\t- test runner output"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0696e093-0770-442b-8dc9-5393bbfcd0b6","uuid":"741f1be2-d4b1-498a-b4fc-a083afc6455e","timestamp":"2026-05-17T13:03:35.255Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md","content":"- retrieval alignment\n\nDo not build opaque autonomous self-rewriting memory. Reflection should be inspectable, testable, and reversible.\n\n## Non-Negotiable Product Properties\n\n- Local-first by default.\n- Deterministic identities for every file, symbol, doc section, event, and memory.\n- Every durable memory has evidence.\n- Every retrieved memory has an inclusion reason.\n- Every stale or contradicted memory is surfaced as such, not hidden behind recency.\n- Every workflow bundle is compact by default with deliberate expansion handles.\n- Every background consolidation pass is recoverable, replayable, and observable.\n- Every public MCP contract is documented and regression-tested.\n- No silent broad workspace reads that bypass ignore rules or workspace boundaries.\n- No unbounded graph traversal, payload growth, or event-log scans on hot paths.\n\n## System Architecture\n\n### 1. Ingestion Layer\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n- watch workspace changes\n- parse code\n- parse docs\n- parse config and build files\n- ingest test results and diagnostics\n- capture assistant event traces\n- normalize all inputs into stable records\n\nRequired inputs:\n\n- source files\n- Markdown docs\n- repo instruction files\n- test files and test manifests\n- package/build metadata\n- compiler diagnostics\n- test runner output","numLines":40,"startLine":85,"totalLines":969}}}
