{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013mQCzwVd8k6QrvKuYzX3ML","type":"tool_result","content":"899\t## Risks\n900\t\n901\t### Opaque Memory Mutation\n902\t\n903\tRisk: automatic consolidation corrupts durable repo knowledge.\n904\t\n905\tControl: event-backed proposals, reversible updates, provenance, review queue for high-scope changes, and replay.\n906\t\n907\t### Ranking Complexity\n908\t\n909\tRisk: ranking becomes hard to reason about.\n910\t\n911\tControl: keep ranker feature-based and inspectable before any learned policy. Expose diagnostic scores.\n912\t\n913\t### Event Log Growth\n914\t\n915\tRisk: event storage becomes too large or slow.\n916\t\n917\tControl: append compact summaries on hot paths, spill large payloads, index by task/session/workspace, and support compaction snapshots.\n918\t\n919\t### Stale Memory Leakage\n920\t\n921\tRisk: agents trust outdated memory.\n922\t\n923\tControl: freshness indexes, graph-change-triggered verification, stale labels in all memory surfaces, and tests that stale memory cannot rank as trusted.\n924\t\n925\t### Scope Leakage\n926\t\n927\tRisk: user/org/branch memories leak into wrong workspaces.\n928\t\n929\tControl: scope-aware queries, enforced filters in store APIs, and negative tests.\n930\t\n931\t### Overfitting To Current Repo\n932\t\n933\tRisk: benchmarks pass only for Lattice-like Rust/TypeScript repos.\n934\t\n935\tControl: fixture repos across languages, repo sizes, and documentation styles.\n936\t\n937\t## First Implementation Slice\n938\t\n939\tThe first real slice should be event log plus memory graph, not UI.\n940\t\n941\tImplement in this order:\n942\t\n943\t1. Event model and append-only store.\n944\t2. MCP workflow event capture.\n945\t3. Memory graph schema and migration/import from existing rows.\n946\t4. Memory access/use history.\n947\t5. Retrieval V1 with graph-aware memory ranking.\n948\t6. Compact memory inclusion reasons in existing workflow tools."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0696e093-0770-442b-8dc9-5393bbfcd0b6","uuid":"d0597c66-7d4b-4446-b004-63cd764e8342","timestamp":"2026-05-17T13:03:36.229Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md","content":"## Risks\n\n### Opaque Memory Mutation\n\nRisk: automatic consolidation corrupts durable repo knowledge.\n\nControl: event-backed proposals, reversible updates, provenance, review queue for high-scope changes, and replay.\n\n### Ranking Complexity\n\nRisk: ranking becomes hard to reason about.\n\nControl: keep ranker feature-based and inspectable before any learned policy. Expose diagnostic scores.\n\n### Event Log Growth\n\nRisk: event storage becomes too large or slow.\n\nControl: append compact summaries on hot paths, spill large payloads, index by task/session/workspace, and support compaction snapshots.\n\n### Stale Memory Leakage\n\nRisk: agents trust outdated memory.\n\nControl: freshness indexes, graph-change-triggered verification, stale labels in all memory surfaces, and tests that stale memory cannot rank as trusted.\n\n### Scope Leakage\n\nRisk: user/org/branch memories leak into wrong workspaces.\n\nControl: scope-aware queries, enforced filters in store APIs, and negative tests.\n\n### Overfitting To Current Repo\n\nRisk: benchmarks pass only for Lattice-like Rust/TypeScript repos.\n\nControl: fixture repos across languages, repo sizes, and documentation styles.\n\n## First Implementation Slice\n\nThe first real slice should be event log plus memory graph, not UI.\n\nImplement in this order:\n\n1. Event model and append-only store.\n2. MCP workflow event capture.\n3. Memory graph schema and migration/import from existing rows.\n4. Memory access/use history.\n5. Retrieval V1 with graph-aware memory ranking.\n6. Compact memory inclusion reasons in existing workflow tools.","numLines":50,"startLine":899,"totalLines":969}}}
